%I A402432 #14 Nov 21 2026 23:11:25
%S A402432 3,5,11,13,23,89,101,179,1693,1721,1913,3203,8171,25169,28087,64627
%N A402432 Primes p > 2 such that either (4/3)*p# - 1 or (8/3)*p# - 1 is prime, where prime(n)# = A002110(n).
%C A402432 Primes prime(n) such that A402505(n) is prime.
%C A402432 One of (4/3)*p# - 1 and (8/3)*p# - 1 is divisible by 3 and the other one is congruent to 1 modulo 3.
%C A402432 a(17) > 10^5. - _Michael S. Branicky_, Nov 21 2026
%e A402432 8-1 = 7 is prime, so 3 is a term;
%e A402432 2*8*5-1 = 79 is prime, so 5 is a term;
%e A402432 2*8*5*7-1 = 559 = 13*43, so 7 is not a term;
%e A402432 8*5*7*11-1 = 3079 is prime, so 11 is a term;
%e A402432 8*5*7*11*13-1 = 40039 is prime, so 13 is a term;
%e A402432 2*8*5*7*11*13*17-1 = 1361359 = 199*6841, so 17 is not a term;
%e A402432 2*8*5*7*11*13*17*19-1 = 25865839 = 47*550337, so 19 is not a term.
%o A402432 (PARI) my(P=8); forprime(p=5, 1000, P*=p; if(ispseudoprime(P-1) || ispseudoprime(2*P-1), print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A402432 Cf. A002110 (primorials), A102476 (4 times primorials), A402505.
%Y A402432 See A402499 for a list of related sequences.
%K A402432 nonn,more,new
%O A402432 1,1
%A A402432 _Jianing Song_, Nov 18 2026
%E A402432 a(16) from _Michael S. Branicky_, Nov 21 2026
